Just a small thought.

Without consulting spoiler, I can think of at least two "herb"
foodstuffs in nethack: Eucalytpus and wolfsbane. There are probably
more that I've forgotten, and at least one that I've YANIed:
http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_frm/thread/8eb281e805c73914/d8eee9493d0a7250?q=catnip&rnum=1#d8eee9493d0a7250

While you and I would probably be able to recognise eucalytpus quite
quickly (largely due to its use in various smelly balms, potions and
things available in the modern world) it strikes me that your average
nethackish barbarian, samurai or rogue might not be able to tell
various plants and herbs apart so easily. Also, I very much doubt more
than a small percentage of people here would be able to recognise
wolfsbane without reference to some kind of guide.

Therefore I propose that herb-type foodstuffs in nethack should be
randomised and require identification like potions, scrolls and so on.
Healers and rangers would start the game with herbs already
indentified.

This addition would probably be relatively easy to code (recycle
randomise/identify code from other items) and wouldn't break bones.
Meanwhile it would add a tiny bit more challenge and interest to the
game - if only by wasting the occasional ID use - and go some small way
to further differentiating the ranger/healer classes from the others.
It might also encourage the addition of other interesting herbs, herbal
effects and interactions to the game.

